title Domain 2 — Tool Design & MCP (revision mind map)

* Domain 2\nTool Design & MCP

' =================== PART A ===================
** PART A\nTool Design (T1–11)
*** T1 Selection\n**DESCRIPTION = primary routing signal**
**** Semantic match (meaning, not keywords)
**** Re-evaluated fresh EVERY turn
**** 4 outcomes: correct / misroute / no-call / **fallback (safe)**
**** 3 fail modes: vague intent / missing scope / no output
*** T2 Writing descriptions
**** 3 parts: WHAT · WHEN(+not) · RETURNS
**** Negative scoping pushes off look-alikes
*** T3–5 Argument correctness
**** T3 precise schema (typed, described)
**** T4 required-only + **enums** + constraints
**** T5 **strict = constrains generation, not post-reject**
*** T6–7 Failure handling
**** T6 useful errors (for the MODEL: what + next step)
**** T7 retry TRANSIENT only · partial-success (don't fake complete)
*** T8–11 Scope & control
**** T8 **least privilege** — tools per agent
**** T9 heuristics + overlap / hallucinate / over-call
**** T10 tool_choice: auto · any · named · none
**** T11 tool search for large catalogs (find-then-use)

' =================== PART B ===================
** PART B\nMCP (T12–26)
*** T12 What / Why
**** Runs ON http — value = **standardization + discovery**
**** Plug-and-play · **model-agnostic** · config not code
*** Roles
**** Claude REQUESTS · **CLIENT executes** · SERVER holds creds
*** T13 **3 primitives (ownership)**
**** TOOLS = model-controlled
**** RESOURCES = app-controlled (context, given)
**** PROMPTS = user-controlled (human invokes)
*** T14–17 Build & expose
**** T14 docstring->desc · type hints->schema
**** T15 list-tools (discover) + call-tool (execute)
**** T16 resources = read-only URIs (app injects)
**** T17 prompt templates (server-authored, user-run)
*** T18–20 Clients & transports
**** T18 lifecycle: connect -> **HANDSHAKE** -> list -> loop
**** T19 STDIO = local · subprocess · no auth
**** T20 Streamable HTTP = remote/prod · auth · **progress (SSE)**
*** T21–22 Advanced
**** T21 **SAMPLING = server asks model via client** (client keeps key)
**** T22 notifications · roots (dir boundary) · progress
*** T23–24 Scope & prod
**** T23 least privilege at server (no "run command")
**** T24 auth(OAuth) · **protocol vs tool versioning** · reliability
*** T25–26 Built-in vs custom
**** T25 built-ins = SERVER tools (you run no code)
**** T26 built-in if it fits, else custom (your systems)

' =================== SPINE ===================
left side
** ONE-LINE SPINE
*** A: DESCRIPTION routes -> SCHEMA/STRICT validate -> ERRORS/RETRY recover -> SCOPE/choice/search control
*** B: STANDARD interface -> connect/HANDSHAKE -> DISCOVER -> Claude routes -> CLIENT executes -> SERVER runs
*** Thread: a bad description misroutes the SAME whether local, remote, client, server, or MCP tool

@endmindmap
